From 5684a30153c4527735f2d92871781ec32700b8b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:23:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] Video at its own rate with VRR: on NVIDIA the
 driver says whether VRR is on

"Video at its own rate with VRR" judged in the first second of a video whether VRR came on from the
vblanks of the CRTC (drmCrtcGetSequence()). nvidia-drm has none with its defaults (vblank=0): the call
fails, CWinSystemGbm::VrrVideoFlipped() returned at once without counting the flip or reading
VRR_ENABLED back, and CStartCheck said UNMEASURED at 5 s. On an RTX 4080 SUPER
(with a Samsung Odyssey G60SD at 360 and 120 Hz, and an LG C5) every video at its own rate ended
"VRR did not come on: the vblanks of the output could not be read in 5 s ... after 0 flips", while
the kernel said "VTEM: VRR on" for the head: the feature did nothing on any NVIDIA GPU.

- nvidia-drm says it now: NV_VRR_ACTIVE, read-only, of the CRTC (nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9079):
  bit 0 is 1 where NVKMS has VRR active on the head after the flip. CStartCheck::DriverSays() takes it
  after each flip until VRR is judged: the first flip is left out, a 0 after it is DRIVER_OFF at once
  ("the driver says that VRR is not active on the head"), three flips with 1 are FOLLOWS. Where the
  driver says it, the vblanks are not needed; where it does not (amdgpu, i915: no such property), the
  vblanks decide as before; with neither, UNMEASURED as before, fail-closed.
- VrrVideoFlipped() counts a flip that the driver took and reads VRR_ENABLED back before it reads the
  vblanks, so the lines of the log say how many flips there were and what the kernel read back.
- The log line of UNMEASURED says what it is ("the driver gives neither the vblanks of the output nor
  whether VRR is active on it"), and the lines of the judgement say what the driver said.
- The VRR row of the player information said "Not on: the mode follows the video" whenever VRR did not
  come on; on a display without a mode at the video's rate (the G60SD has no mode of 24, 48 or 72 Hz)
  the mode followed nothing. Where the mode the video plays in is no whole multiple of its rate
  (VRR_VIDEO::WholeMultipleOf(), within 200 ppm: 119.999 Hz is not one of 23.976), the row says "Not
  on: no mode at the video's rate" (hades.out.vrr "nomode"; Estuary #54306, in English and in the three
  Spanish languages, one line in each), and the row of the mode under it says the rate it plays at.

Not considered: nvidia-drm with vblank=1, which changes the events and vblank references of every
commit, Dolby Vision's among them. A measure from the time of the out-fence of each flip, where a
driver has neither vblanks nor the property: not taken, as nothing on a GPU has shown it to tell VRR
from a fixed refresh (the drivers without vblanks here are nvidia-drm, which has the property, and
driver 580, whose GPUs have no HDMI VRR).

Checked: the host test (tools/regress/kodi-host/vrr_video_test.cpp) with the cases of the driver,
which does not build against the header before this change; the changed files and the 50 sources that
include them compile with the commands of the image's build; the texts of the row fit it in the four
languages (tools/regress/playerinfo). Not run on a GPU.
